    "Direction Cosines & Ratios: If l, m, n are cosines of angles with coordinate axes, then l² + m² + n² = 1. Ratios a, b, c are proportional to l, m, n.",
    "Collinearity: Two vectors a⃗ and b⃗ are collinear if and only if b⃗ = λ a⃗, or their components are strictly proportional (a₁/b₁ = a₂/b₂ = a₃/b₃).",
    "Scalar (Dot) Product: a⃗ · b⃗ = |a⃗||b⃗| cos θ = a₁b₁ + a₂b₂ + a₃b₃. Two non-zero vectors are perpendicular if and only if a⃗ · b⃗ = 0.",
    "Vector (Cross) Product: a⃗ × b⃗ = (|a⃗||b⃗| sin θ) n̂, computed via 3×3 determinant. Two non-zero vectors are parallel if and only if a⃗ × b⃗ = 0⃗.",
